	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Fast search for Apple Mail, straight from Alfred. Results appear as you type, like Spotlight.

USAGE
  mail jane invoice    search everything: subject, sender, recipients and message preview. All words must match.
  mailfrom jane        sender only (from)
  mailto jane          recipient only (to)
  mailsubject invoice  subject only
  maildate             pick from a list (today, yesterday, last 7 days, this month, …) with Enter or Tab,
                       or type a date: today, yesterday, week, month, 2026-11-18, 18-11-2026, 2026-11 or 2026 (search words may follow)
You can also type prefixes in the main search: mail from:jane invoice, to:jane, subject:invoice, date:2026-11-18, after:2026-11-01, before:2026.

ACTIONS
  Enter           open the message in Mail
  Cmd+Enter       copy the sender's email address
  Cmd+L           large type with the message preview
Unread messages have a dot. Junk and trash are skipped; duplicates from "All Mail" are merged.

REQUIREMENTS
Alfred needs Full Disk Access (System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Full Disk Access) to read Mail's index at ~/Library/Mail. Nothing is written or sent anywhere; the database is opened read-only. Python 3 is required: Homebrew's or Apple's (part of the Command Line Tools). If it is missing, the workflow tells you and Enter starts Apple's installer. Keywords can be changed in the workflow configuration.

NOTES
Only the message preview (first lines) is searched, not the full body. Mail's internal database format differs between macOS versions. The workflow detects the layout and adapts (older layouts open the message file instead of a message link). Developed on macOS 27; older versions are supported on a best-effort basis. If results look wrong, run ./mail_search.py --schema in the workflow folder.

DISCLOSURE
This workflow was created with the help of an AI assistant (Claude by Anthropic) and tested by the author.</string>
